    "designMd": "---\nname: FitOra Owner\ncolors:\n  surface: '#f9f9ff'\n  surface-dim: '#cfdaf2'\n  surface-bright: '#f9f9ff'\n  surface-container-lowest: '#ffffff'\n  surface-container-low: '#f0f3ff'\n  surface-container: '#e7eeff'\n  surface-container-high: '#dee8ff'\n  surface-container-highest: '#d8e3fb'\n  on-surface: '#111c2d'\n  on-surface-variant: '#464652'\n  inverse-surface: '#263143'\n  inverse-on-surface: '#ecf1ff'\n  outline: '#777683'\n  outline-variant: '#c7c5d4'\n  surface-tint: '#4f54b4'\n  primary: '#15157d'\n  on-primary: '#ffffff'\n  primary-container: '#2e3192'\n  on-primary-container: '#9da1ff'\n  inverse-primary: '#c0c1ff'\n  secondary: '#006c49'\n  on-secondary: '#ffffff'\n  secondary-container: '#6cf8bb'\n  on-secondary-container: '#00714d'\n  tertiary: '#3c2300'\n  on-tertiary: '#ffffff'\n  tertiary-container: '#5a3700'\n  on-tertiary-container: '#ec9700'\n  error: '#ba1a1a'\n  on-error: '#ffffff'\n  error-container: '#ffdad6'\n  on-error-container: '#93000a'\n  primary-fixed: '#e1e0ff'\n  primary-fixed-dim: '#c0c1ff'\n  on-primary-fixed: '#04006d'\n  on-primary-fixed-variant: '#373a9b'\n  secondary-fixed: '#6ffbbe'\n  secondary-fixed-dim: '#4edea3'\n  on-secondary-fixed: '#002113'\n  on-secondary-fixed-variant: '#005236'\n  tertiary-fixed: '#ffddb8'\n  tertiary-fixed-dim: '#ffb95f'\n  on-tertiary-fixed: '#2a1700'\n  on-tertiary-fixed-variant: '#653e00'\n  background: '#f9f9ff'\n  on-background: '#111c2d'\n  surface-variant: '#d8e3fb'\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 57px\n    fontWeight: '700'\n    lineHeight: 64px\n    letterSpacing: -0.25px\n  headline-lg:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 32px\n    fontWeight: '600'\n    lineHeight: 40px\n  headline-md:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 28px\n    fontWeight: '600'\n    lineHeight: 36px\n  headline-sm:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 24px\n    fontWeight: '600'\n    lineHeight: 32px\n  title-lg:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 22px\n    fontWeight: '500'\n    lineHeight: 28px\n  title-md:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 16px\n    fontWeight: '500'\n    lineHeight: 24px\n    letterSpacing: 0.15px\n  body-lg:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 16px\n    fontWeight: '400'\n    lineHeight: 24px\n    letterSpacing: 0.5px\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 14px\n    fontWeight: '400'\n    lineHeight: 20px\n    letterSpacing: 0.25px\n  label-lg:\n    fontFamily: JetBrains Mono\n    fontSize: 12px\n    fontWeight: '500'\n    lineHeight: 16px\n    letterSpacing: 0.5px\n  headline-lg-mobile:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 28px\n    fontWeight: '700'\n    lineHeight: 34px\nrounded:\n  sm: 0.25rem\n  DEFAULT: 0.5rem\n  md: 0.75rem\n  lg: 1rem\n  xl: 1.5rem\n  full: 9999px\nspacing:\n  unit: 4px\n  margin-mobile: 16px\n  gutter-mobile: 12px\n  stack-sm: 8px\n  stack-md: 16px\n  stack-lg: 24px\n---\n\n## Brand & Style\nThe design system for this product is rooted in **Corporate Modernism** with a high-performance edge. It balances the authoritative reliability of an enterprise management tool with the kinetic energy of a sports academy. The visual narrative is built on the principles of Material Design 3 (M3), utilizing a \"Management-First\" philosophy that prioritizes data clarity and actionable insights without sacrificing a premium, aspirational feel.\n\nThe emotional response should be one of \"Controlled Vitality.\" The UI feels robust and stable (Indigo) while remaining fresh and growth-oriented (Emerald). High-contrast elements and ample whitespace ensure that owners can navigate complex schedules and financial data with zero cognitive friction.\n\n## Colors\nThe palette utilizes a high-contrast foundation to ensure accessibility and professional rigor.\n- **Primary (Deep Indigo):** Used for key structural elements, primary buttons, and active states to signal authority.\n- **Secondary (Emerald Green):** Applied to success states, growth metrics, and \"active\" sports indicators.\n- **Tertiary (Amber):** Reserved for alerts, pending status, or urgent management notifications.\n- **Neutral/Surface:** A tiered system of cool greys and pure whites. Surfaces use `Neutral 99` (#FAFAFA) for the background to keep the interface feeling airy, while containers use pure white (#FFFFFF) to create a distinct card-based hierarchy.\n\n## Typography\nThis design system employs **Inter** for all primary communication to maintain a neutral, highly legible, and professional tone. For data-heavy contexts\u2014such as athlete IDs, financial figures, or timestamps\u2014**JetBrains Mono** is used as a secondary \"Label\" font to provide a technical, precise aesthetic that aids in scanning lists.\n\nThe type scale is intentionally dense for the management context. Use `Title Medium` for card headers and `Body Medium` for secondary information to maximize information density on mobile screens.\n\n## Layout & Spacing\nThe layout follows a **Fluid Grid** model optimized for mobile-first management. \n- **Grid:** 4-column system on mobile devices.\n- **Safe Zones:** 16px horizontal margins protect content from screen edges.\n- **Rhythm:** An 8pt spatial system (with a 4pt sub-grid for tight components) ensures vertical consistency.\n- **Density:** High-density layouts are preferred for data lists. Use 12px gutters between cards to maximize the number of visible items while maintaining clear separation.\n\n## Elevation & Depth\nIn accordance with Material 3, depth is communicated through **Tonal Layers** rather than heavy shadows.\n- **Surface Level 0 (Background):** #FAFAFA.\n- **Surface Level 1 (Cards/Lists):** Pure white with a subtle 1px stroke (#E2E8F0) and no shadow for a clean, flat look.\n- **Surface Level 2 (FABs/Active Modals):** Uses a soft ambient shadow (Y: 4, Blur: 12, Opacity: 0.08, Color: Indigo) to indicate interactivity.\n- **Scrim:** A 40% opacity Indigo tint is used for background overlays when modals are active.\n\n## Shapes\nThe shape language is \"Professional Soft.\"\n- **Standard Containers:** Use `rounded-md` (0.5rem / 8px) for cards, input fields, and list items. This provides a modern feel without looking overly playful.\n- **Action Elements:** Buttons and Floating Action Buttons (FABs) use `rounded-xl` (1.5rem / 24px) or full pill shapes to stand out against the geometric card-based layout.\n- **Data Indicators:** Small badges or tags use `rounded-sm` (4px) to maximize space for text.\n\n## Components\n- **Floating Action Buttons (FAB):** Following M3, the FAB is a large, rounded-square (or \"squircle\") located in the bottom-right. It should be Primary Indigo with a white icon for high-impact actions like \"New Enrollment.\"\n- **Cards:** Use a \"Elevated-Flat\" style. Pure white background, 1px light-grey border. Headers within cards should use Primary Indigo text for emphasis.\n- **Data Tables/Lists:** Highly condensed. Use JetBrains Mono for numeric values. Alternate row backgrounds are not required; use thin 1px horizontal dividers instead.\n- **Chips:** Used for filtering sports categories (e.g., \"Tennis,\" \"Swimming\"). Emerald Green is used for selected states with a 12% opacity background.\n- **Navigation Bar:** A fixed bottom navigation bar with clear icons and labels. The active state uses a Primary Indigo pill-shaped indicator behind the icon, consistent with M3 standards.\n- **Input Fields:** Outlined style with a 1px border that thickens and changes to Indigo on focus. Labels should float to the top border when active.",
